id: design.cascading-timeouts
kind: design
title: cascading timeouts and inner expiry
aliases: cascading timeouts, inner timeout, timeout nesting
tags: design, timeouts, resilience
questions:
  - how do you nest timeouts without an inner one outliving the outer?
  - when is a timeout actually a cascade trigger?
invariant: An inner timeout must be strictly shorter than the caller's remaining deadline, or it can outlive the caller that already gave up.
answer_30s: Derive each inner timeout from the caller's remaining budget (deadline minus now), never from a fixed round number; when the budget is exhausted, fail fast instead of starting a timer you may not live to meet.
when_to_use:
  - layered callers each bounding a downstream call
  - any recursive or chained timeout setup
failure_modes:
  - a fixed inner timeout larger than the caller's remaining budget
  - starting a timer after the budget is already gone, then waiting on it
related:
  - design.timeouts
  - design.deadline
  - design.timeout-budget
sources:
  - https://sre.google/sre-book/timeouts-and-otherwise/
